---
id: avocado-oil-mashed-potatoes
title: Avocado Oil Mashed Potatoes
category: modular_carb

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 500

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Place @yellow-fleshed-potatoes{425%g} (peeled, cut into 1-inch chunks) in a #saucepan. Cover with cold water by 1 inch and add a heavy pinch of salt. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce to medium and simmer for ~simmer-time{13%min} until fork-tender with no core resistance.

Drain thoroughly in a colander. Return the drained potatoes to the empty hot pot off the heat for ~dry-time{75%sec}, shaking gently, until surface moisture has completely evaporated.

Mash the hot, dry potatoes thoroughly with a hand masher or ricer until smooth.

Drizzle in @avocado-oil{1%tsp} and @partly-skimmed-milk-2pct{0.25%cup} (1/4 cup, warmed). Whip vigorously with a whisk or masher to emulsify the oil into the hot starch.

Stir in @kosher-salt{0.5%tsp}, @garlic-powder{0.25%tsp}, and @black-pepper{0.25%tsp} until evenly seasoned and creamy.

Divide equally into 2 meal prep containers (250 g cooked yield each) and let cool before sealing.
